#VRML V2.0 utf8
# Spring-loaded pin, stand-in. There is no part number behind this yet -- it draws
# the envelope the contact has to fill: solder shoulder on the board, barrel, and a
# crown tip meeting the module's BOOT pad 11.04 mm up (socket body 8.5 + header
# plastic 2.54, both read out of their own STEP models).
#
# Anything with roughly this reach works; what matters when picking one is that it
# stands perpendicular over 11 mm and lands inside a 1.0 mm pad.
#
# VRML units are 0.1 inch, hence millimetres / 2.54. Cylinders are written out as
# prisms because KiCad's VRML reader ignores the Cylinder node.
